; A bare FIXED VALUE as a zero-or-more occurrence target (`[* 5]` — a homogeneous array of the
; constant 5) panics generation in `for_rust_member` (`should not expose Fixed type in member`,
; intermediate/rust_type.rs): the homogeneous-element path asks for a Rust representation of a standalone
; `Fixed`, which has none. The registration-time graceful rejection that owns the TOP-LEVEL shapes
; (`x = 5` / `x = true` / `#6.5(5)` — pinned by the tests/matrix_reject value.number/type2.value
; rows and tests/robustness/tagged_literal.cddl) never sees this position, so the occurrence shape
; still reaches the panic. Same class fires for `[* true]` / `[* "v1"]` / `[* null]`, and for a
; tagged prelude constant (tests/robustness/tagged_prelude_constant.cddl). Surfaced by the
; recombination sweep (src/tests/recombination_tests.rs).
a = [* 5]
